BT /F1 12 Tf 72 720 Td 16 TL (Scaled Dot-Product Attention) ' () ' (We compute attention as softmax\(QK^T / sqrt\(d_k\)\) V. For large values of d_k,) ' (the dot products grow large in magnitude, pushing the softmax function into) ' (regions where it has extremely small gradients. To counteract this effect,) ' (we scale the dot products by 1/sqrt\(d_k\).) ' () ' (Multi-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from) ' (different representation subspaces at different positions.) ' ET
endstream
